// Hexagram texts from "The I Ching: A Beginner's Guide to the 64 Hexagrams" by Gavin
// https://www.youriching.com - shared for non-commercial use with attribution.
// bits: lines from bottom to top, 1 = yang (solid), 0 = yin (broken).
window.ICHING = [
{"n": 1, "name": "Heaven", "pin": "Qián", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111111", "sum": "Hexagram 1 is pure creative force meeting no resistance: sustained, disciplined effort now opens the way, provided the pace stays true to your own timing.", "judg": "Heaven: originating, successful, fruitful, and enduring - the four qualities present at every true beginning.", "img": "Heaven in motion is vigor itself: the wise person draws on this to strengthen themselves without pause.", "lines": [{"t": "Strength still concealed", "x": "A dragon still hidden: do not act yet."}, {"t": "Visible, and seeking counsel", "x": "A dragon appears in the field: it is fruitful to seek out someone of real experience."}, {"t": "Effort through a precarious stretch", "x": "The wise person works all day without rest and stays watchful into the evening; the position is precarious, but there is no fault."}, {"t": "Poised over the depths", "x": "Poised to leap, still over the depths: there is no fault."}, {"t": "Strength fully in its element", "x": "A dragon flies in the sky: it is fruitful to seek out someone of real experience."}, {"t": "Strength that has overreached", "x": "A dragon that has flown too high: there is cause for regret."}], "all": "When every line is moving: a company of dragons appears with no single head among them - good fortune."},
{"n": 2, "name": "Earth", "pin": "Kūn", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000000", "sum": "Hexagram 2 describes pure receptivity: strength that carries and completes rather than initiates, gaining direction and lasting good fortune by following a genuinely trustworthy lead.", "judg": "Great success. Favorable to hold to the steadiness of a mare. When the wise person has somewhere to go, going first brings confusion; following finds a master to serve. Favorable to gain companions in the southwest, to lose them in the northeast. Resting in what is steady and true brings good fortune.", "img": "The condition of the earth is complete receptivity. The wise person carries all things by cultivating a broad and generous character.", "lines": [{"t": "Frost before the ice", "x": "Treading on frost: the hard ice is on its way."}, {"t": "Straight, square, unforced", "x": "Straight, square, and great: without any special effort, nothing fails to be favorable."}, {"t": "Ability held in reserve", "x": "Holding refinement within can be kept true; if called to serve in a ruler's affairs, claim no achievement of one's own, yet bring the work to completion."}, {"t": "The sack tied shut", "x": "The sack drawn shut and tied: no blame, no praise."}, {"t": "Quiet competence, worn plainly", "x": "A yellow lower garment: supreme good fortune."}, {"t": "Contending dragons in the field", "x": "Dragons contend in the open wild; their blood is dark and yellow."}], "all": "When every line appears as six: it is favorable to remain steady and true over the long span of time."},
{"n": 3, "name": "Sprouting", "pin": "Zhūn", "up": "Water", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100010", "sum": "Hexagram 3 shows growth struggling to break through at its very start: real progress is underway, but it asks for patience, allies, and small, well-timed steps rather than force.", "judg": "Sprouting: profound success. It is fruitful to stay true. Do not rush out to act on your own; it is fruitful to appoint a helper.", "img": "Clouds and thunder together: Sprouting. The wise person uses the time to sort and weave the threads of order.", "lines": [{"t": "Standing firm before moving", "x": "Circling like a great boundary stone, unmoving: it is fruitful to stay settled and true, fruitful to appoint a helper."}, {"t": "A suitor mistaken for a threat", "x": "Halting, circling; mounted on horses that only pace in place. It is not a raider but a suitor. The woman stays true and does not accept betrothal; after ten years she accepts."}, {"t": "Chasing without a guide", "x": "Chasing a deer with no gamekeeper to guide the way, one only wanders deeper into the forest. The wise person reads the sign early and lets go; pressing onward brings regret."}, {"t": "Circling, then setting out", "x": "Mounted on horses that pace in place, then setting out to seek a match: going brings good fortune, nothing unfavorable."}, {"t": "Small corrections, not sweeping ones", "x": "The rain and its bounty are held back. Correcting matters in small measure brings good fortune; correcting them all at once brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Exhausted by delay", "x": "Mounted on horses that pace in place, weeping tears of blood, streaming without end."}]},
{"n": 4, "name": "Inexperience", "pin": "Méng", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010001", "sum": "Hexagram 4 shows inexperience seeking a teacher: real clarity comes only when a genuine, sincerely asked question meets patient, well-timed, disciplined instruction rather than repeated doubt.", "judg": "Inexperience: success. It is not I who seeks out the untaught youth; the untaught youth seeks me. The first request is answered plainly; a second or third becomes an imposition, and an imposition is not answered. It is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "Below the mountain a spring comes forth: Inexperience. The wise person acts with resolve and cultivates character through it.", "lines": [{"t": "Rules before freedom", "x": "Opening the untaught mind benefits from clear rules and consequence, as one loosens fetters and shackles; pressing forward from there without further correction brings regret."}, {"t": "Patience holds the center", "x": "Embracing the untaught with patience brings good fortune. Taking a wife brings good fortune. A son proves able to manage the household."}, {"t": "Attraction misreads status", "x": "Do not take this woman in marriage: she sees a man of wealth and loses possession of herself. Nothing gained is worthwhile."}, {"t": "Isolated from correction", "x": "Bound in ignorance, cut off from help: regret."}, {"t": "Openness invites the answer", "x": "The inexperienced youth, open and unassuming: good fortune."}, {"t": "Discipline that protects, not conquers", "x": "Striking against ignorance: it does not favor raiding, it favors guarding against raiders."}]},
{"n": 5, "name": "Patience", "pin": "Xū", "up": "Water", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111010", "sum": "Patience asks you to wait at a safe distance from real danger, gathering strength and clarity until the moment is ready to be met.", "judg": "Patience: sincerity brings brightness and success. Staying true brings good fortune. It is fruitful to cross the great river.", "img": "Clouds rise above heaven: Patience. The wise person eats, drinks, and takes rest, keeping body and spirit ready for what is still gathering.", "lines": [{"t": "Held far from danger", "x": "Held in the open country. It is fruitful to hold a constant course. No blame."}, {"t": "Held on uncertain ground", "x": "Held on the sandbank. Some minor talk arises, but the end is good fortune."}, {"t": "Held on unstable footing", "x": "Held in the mud. This draws the raiders near."}, {"t": "Held under real pressure", "x": "Held amid bloodshed. One climbs out from the pit."}, {"t": "Held with composure", "x": "Held over wine and food. Staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "The pause reaches its limit", "x": "Entering the pit. Three uninvited guests arrive; treating them with respect brings good fortune in the end."}]},
{"n": 6, "name": "Dispute", "pin": "Sòng", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010111", "sum": "Hexagram 6 describes a standoff between two forces moving apart: it warns against pressing a grievance to the bitter end and favors settling early through a trusted mediator.", "judg": "Dispute: sincerity is present, yet it meets obstruction and calls for caution. Fortune favors the middle course; carrying the matter all the way to the end brings misfortune. It is fruitful to consult a person of real standing; it is not advantageous to cross the great river.", "img": "Heaven and water move in opposing directions: this is Dispute. The wise person plans thoroughly at the very start of any undertaking, before competing interests can harden into open dispute.", "lines": [{"t": "Let the small friction pass", "x": "Do not let the matter drag on. Some small criticism follows, but in the end, good fortune."}, {"t": "Withdraw before it spreads", "x": "He cannot win the dispute; he withdraws and goes into hiding. The three hundred households of his town are spared any harm."}, {"t": "Hold the line you inherited", "x": "Living on inherited merit, holding to what is right through danger, brings good fortune in the end. If he takes up another's cause, no credit comes to him for it."}, {"t": "Turn back toward what is right", "x": "He cannot win the dispute. He turns back, submits to what is right, changes course, and settles into steadiness: good fortune."}, {"t": "Judgment from true center", "x": "Dispute resolved from a position of true center: supreme good fortune."}, {"t": "A win that will not hold", "x": "Perhaps he is awarded a ceremonial sash for the victory; before the morning is over, it is stripped from him three times."}]},
{"n": 7, "name": "Troops", "pin": "Shī", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010000", "sum": "Hexagram 7 asks you to organize scattered effort under one disciplined leader and one clear rule before any campaign, conflict, or shared project can succeed.", "judg": "Troops: staying true. Good fortune comes when an experienced, mature leader takes command; there is no fault in this.", "img": "Within the earth lies water: Troops. The wise person accordingly gathers the people and cares for the multitude, holding strength in reserve.", "lines": [{"t": "Discipline before the first step", "x": "A force sets out under strict discipline; without that discipline, even a good cause turns to misfortune."}, {"t": "Authority held at the center", "x": "The commander holds the center of the force: good fortune, no fault. The ruler confers authority on him three times over."}, {"t": "A command divided fails", "x": "The force may return carrying its dead in the baggage carts: misfortune."}, {"t": "A disciplined withdrawal", "x": "The force withdraws and camps to the rear: no fault."}, {"t": "Naming the right leader", "x": "Game has entered the field; it is fruitful to state the charge plainly and give pursuit: no fault. Let the elder, capable son lead the troops; if a lesser, untested son shares command, the carts will carry home the dead - persisting in this brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Reward matched to merit", "x": "The great ruler issues his commands: some are granted states to found, others households to inherit; the small-minded must not be employed in either."}]},
{"n": 8, "name": "Alliance", "pin": "Bǐ", "up": "Water", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000010", "sum": "Hexagram 8 describes a bond that holds because it is chosen freely and confirmed early, not one enforced by rank, habit, or fear of standing alone.", "judg": "Alliance: good fortune. Divine again from the source: lasting rightness brings no blame. Those still unsettled will come to join; whoever arrives last meets misfortune.", "img": "Water rests on the earth: Alliance. The ancient kings founded their many states on this pattern, drawing close to their regional lords.", "lines": [{"t": "Sincerity fills the jar", "x": "Sincerity present: joining in alliance brings no blame. Let sincerity fill the jar to its brim, and in the end unexpected good fortune arrives."}, {"t": "Loyalty from within", "x": "Alliance formed from within: staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "The wrong company", "x": "Allying with those who are not the right people."}, {"t": "Alliance offered from outside", "x": "Alliance formed outward: staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Leadership with an open door", "x": "Alliance made visible. The king hunts on three sides only, letting the game ahead escape; the people of the town need no warning. Good fortune."}, {"t": "An alliance without a head", "x": "Alliance without a head: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 9, "name": "Small Accumulation", "pin": "Xiǎoxù", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111011", "sum": "Small Accumulation asks you to build strength through small, steady gains while a larger release of energy is still gathering and cannot yet break through.", "judg": "Small Accumulation: success. Dense clouds gather, yet no rain falls; they move in from our western outskirts.", "img": "Wind moves across the heavens: Small Accumulation. The wise person refines conduct and cultivates virtue through what is graceful and well made.", "lines": [{"t": "Returning to one's own path", "x": "Returning by one's own proper path - what fault could there be? Good fortune."}, {"t": "Drawn back together", "x": "Drawn back by another, returning together. Good fortune."}, {"t": "Forcing the cart forward", "x": "The cart's spokes come loose; husband and wife turn their eyes from each other in anger."}, {"t": "Sincerity dissolves danger", "x": "Sincerity is present: bloodshed departs, and apprehension gives way. No blame."}, {"t": "Shared wealth, bound together", "x": "Sincerity binds firmly together; wealth is shared freely with one's neighbors."}, {"t": "The moon nearly full", "x": "The rain has fallen and settled; accumulated virtue now carries its full load. The one who stays true must still watch for danger, as the moon draws near to full. Pressing forward now brings misfortune."}]},
{"n": 10, "name": "Treading", "pin": "Lǚ", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110111", "sum": "Treading asks you to walk carefully beside real risk, keeping your footing and your manners exact even while something dangerous stays close behind.", "judg": "Treading: one treads on a tiger's tail, and the tiger does not bite. This brings success.", "img": "Heaven above, the lake below: Treading. The wise person distinguishes high from low and settles the resolve of the people.", "lines": [{"t": "Plain conduct at the outset", "x": "Treading in plainness, one goes forward: no blame."}, {"t": "The level, quiet road", "x": "Treading a level, easy road: a person who keeps to quiet retirement finds good fortune through staying true."}, {"t": "Overconfidence invites the bite", "x": "A one-eyed man thinks he can see; a lame man thinks he can walk well."}, {"t": "Careful resolve near real danger", "x": "Treading on the tiger's tail with caution and care: in the end, good fortune."}, {"t": "Decisive footing under danger", "x": "Treading with decisive resolve: even while holding to what is right, there is danger."}, {"t": "Reviewing the completed path", "x": "Look back over the path trodden and examine the signs it left; if the return is complete, great good fortune."}]},
{"n": 11, "name": "Peace", "pin": "Tài", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111000", "sum": "Peace describes a season when opposing forces meet and exchange freely, so small effort now sustains a harmony that still needs tending to last.", "judg": "Peace: the small departs and the great arrives. Good fortune and success.", "img": "Heaven and earth exchange: Peace. Rulers of old shaped this exchange into order, assisted what was fitting in it, and so guided the people.", "lines": [{"t": "Rising together at the root", "x": "Pulling up reed grass, root and all together. Advancing brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Bold, undivided crossing", "x": "Embracing what is uncultivated, daring to cross the river without a boat, not neglecting what is distant, letting go of factions - one is honored for holding the middle path."}, {"t": "Hardship inside a smooth season", "x": "No level ground stays level forever; no departure goes without a return."}, {"t": "Descending without waiting to be ready", "x": "Fluttering downward, not waiting to be rich before joining the neighbors, trusting without being warned."}, {"t": "A costly gesture that secures trust", "x": "The sovereign Yi gives his younger sister in marriage; this brings blessing and great good fortune."}, {"t": "The wall falls into the moat", "x": "The city wall collapses back into the moat. Do not use troops. Issue orders only within one's own town; even with steadiness, there is regret."}]},
{"n": 12, "name": "Obstruction", "pin": "Pǐ", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000111", "sum": "Hexagram 12 describes an obstruction where those who should meet are drifting apart, and the honest response is to withdraw your ambition quietly rather than force a connection that will not hold.", "judg": "Obstruction: this is no way for people to live. It does not favor the steadfastness of the noble one. The great departs; the small arrives.", "img": "Heaven and earth do not exchange: Obstruction. The noble one uses frugal virtue to avoid danger, and does not seek honor through rank or pay.", "lines": [{"t": "Withdraw together, honestly", "x": "Pulling up sacred grass, roots tangled with its own kind: staying true brings good fortune and success."}, {"t": "Compliance is not success", "x": "Bearing up and deferring: good fortune for the small-minded, but the great person keeps to obstruction and calls that success."}, {"t": "Carrying the shame", "x": "Bearing up under shame."}, {"t": "A mandate worth trusting", "x": "Holding a true mandate: no blame. Those bound to you attach themselves to good fortune."}, {"t": "Vigilance ties it to the root", "x": "Bringing obstruction to rest: good fortune for the great person. “It may yet fail, it may yet fail” - tie it fast to the thick mulberry root."}, {"t": "Obstruction turns to joy", "x": "Overturning obstruction: first blockage, then joy."}]},
{"n": 13, "name": "Fellowship", "pin": "Tóngrén", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101111", "sum": "Hexagram 13 asks you to join with others in the open, on shared and honest terms, rather than retreating into a narrow circle of family or faction.", "judg": "Fellowship: joining with others in the open country brings success. It is fruitful to cross the great river; it is fruitful for the wise person to hold firmly to what is right.", "img": "Heaven together with Fire: Fellowship. The wise person accordingly sorts people by their kind and distinguishes things by their category, so that real fellowship can be told apart from mere closeness.", "lines": [{"t": "Open at the very first meeting", "x": "Fellowship begins right at the gate, open to whoever passes: no fault."}, {"t": "Fellowship kept too close", "x": "Fellowship narrowed to one's own clan alone: this brings regret."}, {"t": "A hidden rivalry stalls the alliance", "x": "Arms lie hidden in the thicket, and the watcher climbs a high mound to look out; for three years nothing comes of the ambush."}, {"t": "Standing down from a claim", "x": "He climbs onto the rampart but does not carry the attack through: good fortune."}, {"t": "Reunion earned through struggle", "x": "In fellowship, there is first loud weeping and afterward laughter; a great force prevails, and the two at last meet."}, {"t": "Fellowship kept at a distance", "x": "Fellowship kept out at the meadow, at a distance from the center: no regret."}]},
{"n": 14, "name": "Great Possession", "pin": "Dàyǒu", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111101", "sum": "Hexagram 14 describes abundance held openly under one clear standard: real possession is only secure when what you hold is shared, seen, and used well.", "judg": "Great Possession: supreme success.", "img": "Fire rests high above Heaven: Great Possession. The wise person checks what is wrong, raises up what is good, and follows the good fortune that Heaven has already given.", "lines": [{"t": "No harm before contact", "x": "No dealings yet, so no harm; this is not a fault. Treat the position as difficult and there is no fault."}, {"t": "A load worth carrying", "x": "A great cart carries the load. There is somewhere to go: no fault."}, {"t": "Offered upward, not kept", "x": "A duke presents his offering to the Son of Heaven; a small-minded person could not carry this through."}, {"t": "Strength without a summons", "x": "Not sounding the drum to claim the crowd: no fault."}, {"t": "Sincerity holds the center", "x": "Sincerity draws others to exchange with you; carry dignity as well, and there is good fortune."}, {"t": "Favor from beyond effort", "x": "Help comes from Heaven itself: good fortune, nothing that does not favor you."}]},
{"n": 15, "name": "Humility", "pin": "Qiān", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001000", "sum": "Humility asks you to keep a mountain of substance quietly held within, giving where there is excess and receiving where there is lack, until the whole stays level.", "judg": "Humility: success. The wise person carries it through to the end.", "img": "Within the earth there is a mountain: Humility. The wise person reduces what is excessive and adds to what is deficient, weighing all things and distributing them evenly.", "lines": [{"t": "Humble at the start", "x": "Modest, and modest again: the wise person is fit to cross the great river."}, {"t": "A humility that speaks", "x": "Humility voiced aloud. Staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "The one who carries the load", "x": "Laboring with humility: the wise person carries it through to the end."}, {"t": "Extending humility outward", "x": "Nothing but gain: humility extended and freely given."}, {"t": "Plain authority, real correction", "x": "Not wealthy, yet drawing the neighbors close by it. It is fruitful to move against transgression. Nothing but gain."}, {"t": "A call with little left", "x": "Humility voiced aloud. It is fruitful to march the troops and set one's own towns and lands in order."}]},
{"n": 16, "name": "Anticipation", "pin": "Yù", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000100", "sum": "Hexagram 16 shows momentum built through one clear, trusted mover: readiness and shared eagerness carry a group forward, but only when timing and sincerity align.", "judg": "Anticipation: it is fruitful to establish leaders and to mobilize an army.", "img": "Thunder bursts out of the earth and stirs: Anticipation. The ancient kings composed music to honor virtue, and offered it richly to the highest power, joining it to the memory of their ancestors.", "lines": [{"t": "Excitement announced too soon", "x": "Anticipation announced aloud: misfortune."}, {"t": "Firm judgment, decided quickly", "x": "Firm as stone, deciding before the day is done: staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Watching another's ease", "x": "Gazing upward toward another's ease: regret. Hesitating over it also brings regret."}, {"t": "The one trustworthy center", "x": "The source of anticipation: great gain. Hold no doubt - companions gather to you like a clasp binding hair."}, {"t": "Enduring a weakened position", "x": "A persistent weakness while holding to what is right: it does not end in death."}, {"t": "Waking from a late excitement", "x": "Anticipation kept in the dark: what has already taken shape can still be changed. No blame."}]},
{"n": 17, "name": "Following", "pin": "Suí", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100110", "sum": "Following asks you to move with what is genuinely worth joining, adapting to timing and circumstance without losing your own sense of direction.", "judg": "Following: supreme success. It is fruitful to stay true. No blame.", "img": "Thunder rests within the lake: Following. As evening falls, the wise person goes indoors and settles into rest.", "lines": [{"t": "Leadership shifts, meet it directly", "x": "The one in charge changes course. Staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Choosing novelty over substance", "x": "Bound to the young one, one loses the mature man."}, {"t": "A deliberate, correct choice", "x": "Bound to the mature man, one loses the young one. In following, what is sought is found. It is fruitful to remain settled and true."}, {"t": "A gain that must stay honest", "x": "In following, one gains something, yet persisting in it brings danger."}, {"t": "Sincerity toward what is excellent", "x": "Sincerity toward what is excellent: good fortune."}, {"t": "Binding taken to its furthest point", "x": "Bound fast, then tied still further. The king makes an offering at the Western Mountain."}]},
{"n": 18, "name": "Corruption", "pin": "Gǔ", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011001", "sum": "Hexagram 18 describes decay that has set in through neglect, and the patient, sometimes uncomfortable work of repairing it before it spreads further.", "judg": "Corruption: great success. It is fruitful to cross the great river. Three days before the starting day, three days after it.", "img": "Wind gathers, trapped at the foot of the mountain: Corruption. The wise person rouses the people and cultivates virtue in response.", "lines": [{"t": "Taking up unfinished business", "x": "Repairing the father's decay: with a capable child to take it on, the departed father is freed from blame. There is danger, but in the end, good fortune."}, {"t": "Correcting without force", "x": "Repairing the mother's decay: one should not press for rigid correction."}, {"t": "Some regret, no real fault", "x": "Repairing the father's decay: some slight regret, but no great blame."}, {"t": "Tolerating what should be fixed", "x": "Tolerating the father's decay without correcting it: going forward brings difficulty."}, {"t": "Repair that earns honor", "x": "Repairing the father's decay: it earns honor."}, {"t": "Beyond the work of office", "x": "Serving neither king nor lord, holding instead to a higher work."}]},
{"n": 19, "name": "Drawing Near", "pin": "Lín", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110000", "sum": "Hexagram 19 describes a strong, benevolent presence drawing near to guide others, its influence growing while still gentle enough to earn trust rather than command it.", "judg": "Drawing near: great success. It is fruitful to stay true. By the eighth month, there will be misfortune.", "img": "Earth rests above the lake: Drawing Near. The wise person teaches without end and shelters the people without limit.", "lines": [{"t": "Sincerity at the first step", "x": "Drawing near through genuine feeling: staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Feeling proven by steadiness", "x": "Drawing near through genuine feeling: good fortune, nothing that is not favorable."}, {"t": "Sweetness without substance", "x": "Drawing near through flattering sweetness: nothing favorable. Once this is met with honest concern, there is no blame."}, {"t": "A complete, unhesitating step", "x": "Drawing near completely, without reserve: no blame."}, {"t": "Authority earned through understanding", "x": "Drawing near through wisdom: fitting conduct for a great ruler, good fortune."}, {"t": "Generosity at the furthest reach", "x": "Drawing near with generous sincerity: good fortune, no blame."}]},
{"n": 20, "name": "Observation", "pin": "Guān", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000011", "sum": "Hexagram 20 asks you to step back and watch carefully before acting, because what you see clearly now will shape whether your next move is trusted or resisted.", "judg": "Observation: like the moment of purification before the offering is presented, not yet the act itself. Sincerity held with quiet dignity commands attention.", "img": "Wind moves over the earth: Observation. The ancient kings surveyed the regions, observed the people, and shaped their teaching accordingly.", "lines": [{"t": "A child's narrow view", "x": "A child's view: seeing only what is near and simple. For an ordinary bystander this brings no blame, but for someone who should know better, it is a source of regret."}, {"t": "Watching through a crack", "x": "Peering through a crack: a narrow, partial view. It is fitting for one who must stay cautious and watch from within, but it should not be mistaken for full understanding."}, {"t": "Self-examination decides direction", "x": "Observe your own conduct to decide whether to advance or withdraw."}, {"t": "Drawn toward visible excellence", "x": "Observe the brilliance of the realm: it is fitting to be received as a guest at the court. Being close to what is admirable opens the way to serve it."}, {"t": "Your own life as the model", "x": "Observe your own conduct as the one others watch. For a person of integrity this brings no blame, because the example given matches the position held."}, {"t": "A pattern that outlasts the role", "x": "Observe the conduct that flows from your life, even after direct authority has passed. For a person of integrity this still brings no blame, since the pattern set continues to be seen."}]},
{"n": 21, "name": "Jaws Closing", "pin": "Shìkè", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100101", "sum": "Hexagram 21 shows an obstruction lodged between the jaws that must be bitten through decisively before it can be swallowed and resolved.", "judg": "Jaws Closing: success. It is fruitful to use the courts - to bring a matter to a clear ruling.", "img": "Thunder and lightning: Jaws Closing. The ancient kings made penalties clear and set the laws in order.", "lines": [{"t": "A light clamp, caught early", "x": "A wooden clamp is fitted over the foot, covering the toes: no blame."}, {"t": "Biting deep into soft resistance", "x": "The teeth sink through soft flesh until it covers the nose: no blame."}, {"t": "A tainted bite, held firm", "x": "Chewing dried meat, the jaw meets a tainted spot: mild embarrassment, but no blame."}, {"t": "Hard evidence found in the bite", "x": "Chewing dried meat still on the bone, a bronze arrowhead is found inside: it is fruitful to hold firm through hardship; good fortune."}, {"t": "A costly ruling, rightly made", "x": "Chewing dried meat, yellow gold is found within: to persevere is dangerous work, yet there is no blame."}, {"t": "A heavy, overdue reckoning", "x": "A wooden yoke is fitted over the neck, covering the ears: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 22, "name": "Adornment", "pin": "Bì", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101001", "sum": "Adornment favors modest success: decoration and presentation can support a worthy matter, but only substance underneath makes a large undertaking sound.", "judg": "Adornment: success. There is small advantage in having somewhere to go.", "img": "Fire at the foot of the mountain: Adornment. The wise person clarifies the ordinary business of governing, yet dares not decide a criminal case on appearance alone.", "lines": [{"t": "Choosing the plainer way", "x": "Adorning his toes. He gives up the carriage and goes on foot."}, {"t": "Ornament that follows the substance", "x": "Adorning his beard."}, {"t": "Adorned, at risk of staining", "x": "Adorned and moistened. Lasting constancy brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Plain sincerity, mistaken for a threat", "x": "Adorned yet plain, white as an undyed cloth. A white horse comes flying swift. This is no raider - it is a suitor come to marry."}, {"t": "A modest gift, sincerely given", "x": "Adornment in the hill garden. The bundled silks are small and few."}, {"t": "Adornment returns to plainness", "x": "Plain, unadorned white. No blame."}]},
{"n": 23, "name": "Stripping Away", "pin": "Bō", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000001", "sum": "Stripping Away describes a structure being worn down from below, layer by layer, until almost nothing solid remains, and it counsels patient restraint rather than a doomed stand.", "judg": "Stripping Away: it is not fruitful to go anywhere.", "img": "The mountain rests on the earth: Stripping Away. Seeing this, those above thicken what is below, so the dwelling can remain secure.", "lines": [{"t": "Erosion begins at the base", "x": "Stripping the bed starting at its legs. To disregard what is true and steady brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Erosion reaches the frame", "x": "Stripping the bed reaches its frame. To disregard what is true and steady brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Standing apart from the drift", "x": "In stripping away, this one is free of blame."}, {"t": "Erosion reaches the skin", "x": "Stripping the bed reaches the skin itself. Misfortune."}, {"t": "Favor rightly distributed", "x": "Fish strung one after another, as palace attendants are led in by favor: nothing is unfavorable."}, {"t": "What survives the erosion", "x": "A single large fruit left uneaten. The noble one obtains a carriage; the petty person strips away their own shelter."}]},
{"n": 24, "name": "Return", "pin": "Fù", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100000", "sum": "Hexagram 24 shows a single new impulse re-entering after a season of decline, small and fragile but pointed the right way, asking to be protected rather than rushed.", "judg": "Return: success. Going out and coming in bring no harm; friends arrive without blame. The way turns back on itself, and in seven days return comes again. It is fruitful to have somewhere to go.", "img": "Thunder lies within the earth: Return. The former kings closed the passes at the solstice, so that merchants and travelers did not journey and rulers did not inspect the outer regions.", "lines": [{"t": "Correcting course early", "x": "Returning before going far: no room even for regret, great good fortune."}, {"t": "Resting near what is good", "x": "Returning to rest near what is good: good fortune."}, {"t": "An unsteady, repeated return", "x": "Returning again and again, unsteady each time: precarious, yet no blame."}, {"t": "Returning alone, mid-path", "x": "Walking the middle way, returning alone, apart from those around."}, {"t": "Generous, settled return", "x": "Returning with generous sincerity: no regret."}, {"t": "Mistaking confusion for return", "x": "Losing the way back and calling it return: misfortune, with calamity from without and error from within. Using this state to move troops ends in great defeat; it brings disaster on the ruler of the state, and for ten years it cannot campaign again."}]},
{"n": 25, "name": "Genuineness", "pin": "Wúwàng", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100111", "sum": "Hexagram 25 shows action that arises without calculation or hidden agenda, so pure of motive that it moves in accord with what is already true.", "judg": "Genuineness: supreme success, and it is fruitful to hold to what is correct. But conduct that is not truly correct brings harm, and it is not fruitful to go forward under those conditions.", "img": "Thunder rolls out under heaven, and every creature is granted its share without pretense. The ancient kings, in rich accord with the season, nourished and raised the many things.", "lines": [{"t": "The first honest step forward", "x": "Genuine action, without pretense: to go forward brings good fortune."}, {"t": "A harvest that was not planned", "x": "Reaping without having plowed, harvesting a rich field without having broken new ground for it: then it is fruitful to go forward."}, {"t": "A loss that was never yours", "x": "An unearned misfortune reaches even the genuine: someone ties an ox nearby, a passing traveler takes it, and the local resident bears the loss."}, {"t": "Quietly holding the correct course", "x": "One may hold firm to what is correct: no blame."}, {"t": "An illness with no medicine needed", "x": "An illness that arrives without cause, despite genuine conduct: do not medicate it, and there will be cause for joy."}, {"t": "Genuine action at the wrong moment", "x": "To act, even genuinely, at this position brings trouble: nothing is gained by moving forward."}]},
{"n": 26, "name": "Great Accumulation", "pin": "Dàxù", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111001", "sum": "Great Accumulation asks you to hold restless strength in reserve, build real capacity through discipline, and release it only when the way is genuinely open.", "judg": "Great Accumulation: it is fruitful to stay true. Not eating at home brings good fortune. It is fruitful to cross the great river.", "img": "Heaven within the Mountain: Great Accumulation. The wise person studies the sayings and deeds of the past in order to build up their own character.", "lines": [{"t": "Danger calls for a full stop", "x": "There is danger; it is fruitful to stop."}, {"t": "The cart withdraws itself", "x": "The cart's axle strap comes loose."}, {"t": "A fine horse, firmly held", "x": "A fine horse gives chase. It is fruitful to stay firm through hardship."}, {"t": "Restrain the danger early", "x": "A young bull wears a crossbar on its horns: great good fortune."}, {"t": "Gentle restraint tames the wild edge", "x": "A gelded boar's tusks: good fortune."}, {"t": "The crossroads of Heaven open", "x": "One shoulders the open crossroads of Heaven: success."}]},
{"n": 27, "name": "Sustenance", "pin": "Yí", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100001", "sum": "Hexagram 27 shows an open mouth between two firm lines, asking what actually nourishes you and whether you earn that nourishment or merely take it.", "judg": "Sustenance: to stay true brings good fortune. Observe how nourishment moves, and watch each one seek their own food.", "img": "Thunder stirs beneath the mountain: Sustenance. The wise person is careful in speech and moderate in eating and drinking.", "lines": [{"t": "Envying another's plate", "x": "You set aside your own sacred tortoise, the means of judging for yourself, and instead watch my jaws move with envious hunger: misfortune."}, {"t": "Reaching upward against the norm", "x": "Nourishment sought upside-down goes against what is proper; turning to the height above for support and pressing forward brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Turning against your own nourishment", "x": "To turn against the very source of nourishment brings misfortune even when held firm; for ten years it can serve no purpose, and nothing is gained."}, {"t": "A tiger's steady watchfulness", "x": "Nourishment given downward here brings good fortune. Watching with a tiger's steady, unblinking gaze, pursuing the need with urgency: no blame."}, {"t": "Holding still under a weak claim", "x": "Going against the usual pattern, yet staying settled and true brings good fortune; it is not the time to cross the great river."}, {"t": "Becoming the source others rely on", "x": "To become the very source others rely on for nourishment is a position of danger, yet good fortune follows; it is fruitful to cross the great river."}]},
{"n": 28, "name": "Great Exceeding", "pin": "Dàguò", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011110", "sum": "Great Exceeding describes a central structure sagging under a weight it cannot fully carry, warning that decisive, even solitary, action is needed before the strain reaches a breaking point.", "judg": "Great Exceeding: the ridgepole sags. It is fruitful to have somewhere to go; this brings success.", "img": "The lake rises over the wood: Great Exceeding. Seeing this, the wise person stands alone without fear, and withdraws from the world without regret.", "lines": [{"t": "Care at the weak foundation", "x": "Laying down white reed grass as a mat beneath the offering. No blame."}, {"t": "An unlikely renewal takes root", "x": "A withered willow sprouts new shoots at the root; an older man takes a young wife. Nothing is unfavorable."}, {"t": "The beam sags under the load", "x": "The ridgepole sags. Misfortune."}, {"t": "The beam arches and holds", "x": "The ridgepole arches upward, holding firm. Good fortune, but there is difficulty from another quarter."}, {"t": "Flowering without lasting praise", "x": "A withered willow puts out flowers; an older woman takes a young husband. No blame, but no praise either."}, {"t": "Wading past the point of safety", "x": "Wading through water so deep it covers the crown of the head."}]},
{"n": 29, "name": "Water", "pin": "Kǎn", "up": "Water", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010010", "sum": "Hexagram 29 is water flowing into a gorge and out again: real danger repeats, but staying true to your own course carries you through it intact.", "judg": "Danger doubled and practiced. When sincerity is genuinely held, the heart finds its way through, and right action is honored.", "img": "Water arrives again and again, filling one gorge after another. The wise person keeps a constant standard of conduct and practices what they teach until it becomes second nature.", "lines": [{"t": "Sinking into the first pit", "x": "In the repeated pit, sinking into its deepest hollow: misfortune."}, {"t": "Danger held, gain kept small", "x": "Within the pit there is real danger; seek only a modest gain for now."}, {"t": "Between two pits, no clear ground", "x": "Coming and going between one pit and the next, danger pressing close on every side, sinking into the deepest hollow: do not act."}, {"t": "A plain offering through the window", "x": "A jar of wine, a simple dish of grain, plain earthen vessels, an offering passed through the window rather than the door: in the end, no fault."}, {"t": "Level ground, not yet full", "x": "The pit is not yet full, but the water has reached level ground: no fault."}, {"t": "Bound among the thorns", "x": "Bound with cords and placed among thorn bushes, not released for three years: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 30, "name": "Fire", "pin": "Lí", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101101", "sum": "Fire has no light of its own; it must cling to fuel and repeat itself to keep burning, so lasting brightness depends on what you attach yourself to, not on intensity alone.", "judg": "Fire: it is fruitful to stay correct. Success. Nurturing a cow brings good fortune.", "img": "Brightness arises twice, one flame after another: Fire. Seeing this, the great one carries the light onward, illuminating every quarter without letting it lapse.", "lines": [{"t": "Careful steps in dazzling ground", "x": "Treading carefully among crisscrossed, dazzling patterns. Showing reverence and care. No blame."}, {"t": "Yellow fire holds the center", "x": "Yellow fire, clinging to the center. Great good fortune."}, {"t": "Facing the fire's own sunset", "x": "The fire of the setting sun. If one does not drum on the jar and sing, then comes the lament of old age. Misfortune."}, {"t": "A blaze that consumes itself", "x": "It comes on so suddenly: burning, dying, cast aside."}, {"t": "Grief that clears the way", "x": "Tears streaming down, grieving and sighing. Good fortune."}, {"t": "A disciplined campaign", "x": "The king uses this to march out on campaign. There is praise for striking down the chief, while those who merely followed are spared. No blame."}]},
{"n": 31, "name": "Influence", "pin": "Xián", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001110", "sum": "Influence begins with receptive attention: attraction becomes meaningful when each side can respond freely, steadily, and without force. Being moved and being right to move are separate questions.", "judg": "Influence: success. It is fruitful to stay true. Taking a wife brings good fortune.", "img": "High on the mountain rests a lake: Influence. The wise person keeps the heart open and receives others without preconception.", "lines": [{"t": "Sensation at the threshold", "x": "Influence reaches the big toe."}, {"t": "Impulse seeks a center", "x": "Influence reaches the calves: misfortune. Staying still brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Desire becomes pursuit", "x": "Influence reaches the thighs; it clings to what it follows. Pressing forward brings regret."}, {"t": "Steadiness shapes the field", "x": "Staying true brings good fortune and regret fades. Restless coming and going: only close companions follow your thoughts."}, {"t": "Quiet influence at the core", "x": "Influence reaches the flesh of the back: no regret."}, {"t": "Words reach their limit", "x": "Influence reaches the jaw, the cheeks, and the tongue."}]},
{"n": 32, "name": "Duration", "pin": "Héng", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011100", "sum": "Duration asks whether a commitment, habit, or bond can hold its course through ordinary time, favoring steady conduct over any single dramatic gesture of loyalty.", "judg": "Duration: success, no error. It is fruitful to stay true, and favorable to have somewhere to go.", "img": "Thunder and wind together: Duration. The wise person stands firm and does not change direction.", "lines": [{"t": "Digging too deep, too soon", "x": "Digging deep too soon for duration: to persist here brings misfortune, and nothing is gained."}, {"t": "Centered without forcing", "x": "Regret disappears."}, {"t": "Virtue that will not hold", "x": "Virtue that will not hold steady may bring shame; to persist in this way invites regret."}, {"t": "Waiting where nothing gathers", "x": "Hunting the field all day, no game is caught."}, {"t": "Constancy in a supporting role", "x": "Holding virtue with constancy: good fortune for a wife, misfortune for a husband."}, {"t": "Restless at the very top", "x": "Shaking constancy at the very end: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 33, "name": "Retreat", "pin": "Dùn", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001111", "sum": "Retreat teaches timely withdrawal: when a small, rising pressure cannot yet be met head-on, the wiser move is a measured, dignified departure.", "judg": "Retreat: it succeeds. In small matters, it is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "Heaven lies far above the mountain: Retreat. The wise person keeps distance from small-minded pressure, firm without contempt.", "lines": [{"t": "Lagging at the rear", "x": "To lag at the tail of a retreat is dangerous. Do not press forward to hold what is already leaving."}, {"t": "A bond that will not loosen", "x": "Bound with a strap of yellow ox-hide, and nothing can loosen it."}, {"t": "Torn between staying and leaving", "x": "Held back by attachment while retreating brings distress and danger; yet tending one's own household still brings good fortune."}, {"t": "A clean, willing release", "x": "A willing retreat: fortunate for the wise person, but not for the small-minded."}, {"t": "Withdrawing with grace", "x": "An admirable retreat, held to what is right: good fortune."}, {"t": "Free and unburdened retreat", "x": "An ample, unburdened retreat: nothing is unfavorable."}]},
{"n": 34, "name": "Great Vigor", "pin": "Dàzhuàng", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111100", "sum": "Great Vigor arrives at the height of its strength and asks whether that strength is disciplined enough to act only on what is right.", "judg": "Great Vigor: it is fruitful to hold to what is right.", "img": "Thunder sounds above heaven: Great Vigor. The wise person will not set a foot on ground that violates propriety.", "lines": [{"t": "Force before footing", "x": "Vigor shows first in the toes. Advancing now brings misfortune, even though sincerity is present."}, {"t": "Strength held at center", "x": "Holding to what is right brings good fortune."}, {"t": "The ram and the hedge", "x": "The small-minded rely on force; the wise person relies on restraint. Even holding correctly is precarious here: a ram butts a hedge and tangles its horns."}, {"t": "The hedge finally gives way", "x": "Holding to what is right brings good fortune and regret fades. The hedge breaks open and no horns are caught; strength now shows in the axle of a great cart."}, {"t": "Letting the ram go", "x": "The ram is let go at the border, without regret."}, {"t": "Trapped by your own power", "x": "A ram butts a hedge, unable to retreat and unable to advance. Nothing is gained by it, yet facing the difficulty honestly brings good fortune."}]},
{"n": 35, "name": "Advance", "pin": "Jìn", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000101", "sum": "Hexagram 35 shows the sun rising above the horizon, a figure of steady, visible advance and recognition that grows out of merit already noticed rather than force.", "judg": "Advance: the accomplished marquis is granted many horses, and is received in audience three times in a single day.", "img": "Light rises above the earth: this is Advance. The wise person thereby makes their own bright virtue shine forth.", "lines": [{"t": "An early advance, not yet trusted", "x": "Advancing, yet held back: to hold steady is fortunate. Trust from above has not yet arrived, but an unhurried, generous bearing brings no blame."}, {"t": "A troubled rise, quietly rewarded", "x": "Advancing, yet troubled: to hold steady is fortunate. A great blessing is received, coming down from the royal grandmother."}, {"t": "Advance trusted by the group", "x": "The multitude gives its trust and joins in: regret disappears."}, {"t": "A rodent blocking the way", "x": "Advancing like a large, hesitant rodent, darting forward and back: to persist this way is dangerous."}, {"t": "Advancing without counting the cost", "x": "Regret disappears. Do not fret over gain or loss: to go forward is fortunate, and nothing is unfavorable."}, {"t": "Advance pressed to its very edge", "x": "Advancing to the very horns: use this force only to correct one's own domain. Danger, yet good fortune and no blame; but to make it the constant rule brings regret."}]},
{"n": 36, "name": "Dimmed Light", "pin": "Míngyí", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101000", "sum": "Hexagram 36 shows light buried under the earth: brightness is real but must be guarded quietly for now, held firm through hardship rather than shown openly.", "judg": "Dimmed Light: favorable to hold firm through hardship.", "img": "The light has entered into the earth: this is Dimmed Light. The wise person, governing others, uses an appearance of obscurity and still sees clearly.", "lines": [{"t": "Wings drooping in flight", "x": "The light dims in flight, its wings drooping low; the wise person presses onward, going three days without food. There is somewhere to travel to, though the host has words of complaint."}, {"t": "A wound that can be carried", "x": "The light is wounded, injured in the left thigh; rescued by a horse strong enough to carry the weight - good fortune."}, {"t": "A deliberate hunt to the south", "x": "Amid the dimmed light, a hunt toward the south captures the great chief responsible for the harm; this cannot be forced through quickly - hold firm."}, {"t": "Reading the true intent, then leaving", "x": "Entering deep on the left side, one grasps the true intent behind the dimmed light, and then withdraws again through the courtyard gate."}, {"t": "Holding firm under a hostile superior", "x": "The dimmed light of the Count of Ji: favorable to hold firm."}, {"t": "Risen high, then fallen into darkness", "x": "No longer merely dim but wholly dark: first risen to the height of heaven, then fallen into the earth."}]},
{"n": 37, "name": "Household", "pin": "Jiārén", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101011", "sum": "Household describes order built from the inside out: a home, a team, or a life holds together when roles are clear, speech has substance, and conduct stays consistent.", "judg": "Household: it is fruitful for the woman to remain constant and true.", "img": "Wind rises out of fire: Household. The wise person speaks with real substance and acts with lasting constancy.", "lines": [{"t": "Boundaries set at the start", "x": "Set clear boundaries for the household from the very start: regret disappears."}, {"t": "Tending the center", "x": "She pursues no separate ambition of her own; tending the meals and the home within, staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Too stern, or too loose", "x": "The household grows stern and exacting: regret and severity, yet in the end good fortune. Wife and children giggle without discipline: in the end, humiliation."}, {"t": "Prosperity through quiet restraint", "x": "The household prospers and grows rich: great good fortune."}, {"t": "Arriving in true form", "x": "The ruler arrives at the household in true and complete form: there is nothing to worry over, good fortune."}, {"t": "Sincerity that lasts", "x": "Sincerity joined with quiet dignity: in the end, good fortune."}]},
{"n": 38, "name": "Opposition", "pin": "Kuí", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110101", "sum": "Hexagram 38 describes real divergence between people or intentions that still share one situation, and counsels small, patient steps rather than one large move to close the gap.", "judg": "Opposition: good fortune in small matters.", "img": "Fire above, lake below: Opposition. The wise person stays joined with others in what is genuinely shared, while keeping what is genuinely different distinct.", "lines": [{"t": "Let the lost horse return", "x": "No regret. The lost horse is not chased - it returns on its own. Meeting a disagreeable person brings no blame."}, {"t": "Meet in the back lane", "x": "He meets his lord in a back lane: no blame."}, {"t": "A hard beginning, a good end", "x": "He sees his cart dragged back and his ox held from moving; the man is branded and his nose is cut off. No good beginning, but a good end."}, {"t": "One trusted ally in isolation", "x": "Isolated in opposition, he meets a great-hearted man; the two trust each other. Danger, yet no blame."}, {"t": "Kin close the distance", "x": "Regret vanishes. His own kin bite through the skin with ease. Going forward, what blame could there be?"}, {"t": "Not a raider, a suitor", "x": "Isolated in opposition, he sees a pig caked in mud, and a cart that looks loaded with ghosts. First he draws his bow against it, then lowers the bow: it is not a raider but someone coming to marry. Going forward and meeting rain brings good fortune."}]},
{"n": 39, "name": "Hardship", "pin": "Jiǎn", "up": "Water", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001010", "sum": "Hardship shows a real obstacle ahead - a mountain with water pooling above it - and asks you to turn inward and correct your own stance before advancing.", "judg": "Hardship: it is fruitful to go southwest; it is not fruitful to go northeast. It is fruitful to see the great person. Holding to what is right brings good fortune.", "img": "Water lies above the mountain: Hardship. The wise person turns inward and cultivates their own character.", "lines": [{"t": "Praise for turning back", "x": "Going forward meets hardship; coming back earns praise."}, {"t": "Loyalty inside real difficulty", "x": "The king's minister meets hardship upon hardship, not for any fault of their own."}, {"t": "A second warning to turn back", "x": "Going forward meets hardship; it is better to turn back."}, {"t": "Joining others in hardship", "x": "Going forward meets hardship; coming back joins with others."}, {"t": "Companions answer great hardship", "x": "Great hardship, yet companions arrive."}, {"t": "A substantial return", "x": "Going forward meets hardship; coming back brings something substantial. Good fortune. It is fruitful to see the great person."}]},
{"n": 40, "name": "Release", "pin": "Jiě", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010100", "sum": "Release marks the moment accumulated difficulty finally breaks open into relief - good fortune comes from returning to ordinary life quickly and acting early on whatever genuinely still remains.", "judg": "Release: it is fruitful to go toward the southwest. If there is nowhere further to go, returning brings good fortune; if there is somewhere to go, going early brings good fortune.", "img": "Thunder and rain arise: Release. The wise person pardons faults and forgives offenses.", "lines": [{"t": "Stillness before the knot loosens", "x": "No blame."}, {"t": "Clearing the hidden foxes", "x": "In the field he catches three foxes and obtains a yellow arrow: staying true brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Riding above your station", "x": "Carrying a burden on the back while riding in a carriage invites robbers: persisting brings regret."}, {"t": "Freeing the small attachment", "x": "Free yourself from the big toe, and companions arrive in good faith."}, {"t": "Sincerity that reaches the small-minded", "x": "The wise person achieves deliverance: good fortune. Sincerity reaches even the small-minded."}, {"t": "The decisive shot from the wall", "x": "The duke shoots a hawk perched on the high wall and takes it: nothing but gain."}]},
{"n": 41, "name": "Decrease", "pin": "Sǔn", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110001", "sum": "Decrease asks you to give up something at the base so that what truly matters higher up can be strengthened and trusted.", "judg": "Decrease: with sincerity, there is great good fortune and no blame. Staying true is possible, and it is fruitful to have somewhere to go. What need is there for elaborate offerings? Two plain bowls are enough for the sacrifice.", "img": "A lake lies beneath the mountain: Decrease. The wise person checks anger before it spreads and restrains desire before it multiplies.", "lines": [{"t": "Finish, then release", "x": "When the task at hand is finished, move on quickly: no blame. Weigh carefully how much should be given up, then give up only that much."}, {"t": "Hold your ground", "x": "Staying true brings benefit; advancing brings misfortune. Do not reduce yourself here - holding steady is itself the true increase."}, {"t": "One loyalty, not three", "x": "Three walking together must lose one companion; one walking alone gains a true friend."}, {"t": "Relief through reduction", "x": "Reduce the affliction, and let relief arrive without delay: no blame."}, {"t": "Accept the gift plainly", "x": "Someone enriches this position with a tortoise shell worth ten pairs of currency; no one can refuse such a gift - great good fortune."}, {"t": "Give without keeping score", "x": "Not decreasing but increasing others: no blame, and staying true brings good fortune. It is fruitful to have somewhere to go; one gains devoted service from those who no longer count private gain as home."}]},
{"n": 42, "name": "Increase", "pin": "Yì", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100011", "sum": "Increase describes a moment when what is above willingly gives to what is below, so growth becomes real only through honest, well-timed action.", "judg": "Increase: it is favorable to have a direction to go, favorable to cross the great river.", "img": "Wind and thunder together: Increase. The wise person, seeing good, moves toward it, and, seeing fault in themselves, corrects it.", "lines": [{"t": "A bold start earns its gain", "x": "It is favorable to undertake great work: supreme good fortune, no blame."}, {"t": "An unrefusable gift, held with integrity", "x": "Someone increases him with a tortoise shell worth ten pairs of cowries, and he cannot refuse it. Lasting steadfastness brings good fortune. The king makes offering to the Supreme Being: good fortune."}, {"t": "Gain spent on a real emergency", "x": "Increase is used to meet a calamity: no blame. Holding good faith and walking the middle path, one reports to the duke bearing the ceremonial jade tablet."}, {"t": "Consensus enables a major move", "x": "Walking the middle path, one reports to the duke and is followed: it is favorable to rely on this to move the capital."}, {"t": "Generosity that needs no proof", "x": "Holding good faith and a generous heart, there is no need to ask: supreme good fortune. Good faith answers my own generous conduct."}, {"t": "Resolve that will not hold", "x": "No one increases him; someone may even strike him. His resolve is not constant: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 43, "name": "Breakthrough", "pin": "Guài", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Heaven", "bits": "111110", "sum": "Breakthrough describes a decision that has essentially already been made, five gathered strengths facing one final holdout, calling for the matter to be proclaimed openly rather than forced through in private.", "judg": "Breakthrough: proclaimed openly at the royal court, with a sincere warning cry. There is danger. Announce it within your own city; it does not favor resorting to arms. It is fruitful to have somewhere to go.", "img": "The lake rises above heaven: Breakthrough. Seeing this, the wise person extends generosity down to those below, and takes care never to settle comfortably into virtue already claimed.", "lines": [{"t": "Premature strength at the toes", "x": "Strength surges into the forward toes; advancing before it can prevail brings blame."}, {"t": "A wary cry needs no fear", "x": "A wary, warning cry: even should raiders come in the dead of night, there is nothing to fear."}, {"t": "Decisive despite quiet attachment", "x": "Strength shows in the cheekbones; there is danger. Yet the noble one decides and decides again - walking alone, caught in rain and soaked through, feeling resentment, but incurring no blame."}, {"t": "A hesitant step needs guidance", "x": "The buttocks are without skin, and walking becomes halting; leading a goat along from behind, regret vanishes, yet hearing this advice, no one believes it."}, {"t": "Easy resolve on open ground", "x": "Like a thin-horned goat crossing open pasture, deciding and deciding again; walking the middle way brings no blame."}, {"t": "No one left to call on", "x": "No one left to cry out to; in the end, misfortune comes."}]},
{"n": 44, "name": "Encounter", "pin": "Gòu", "up": "Heaven", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011111", "sum": "Encounter shows a single yielding line rising to meet five firm ones below the sky - an unplanned meeting that carries real influence and asks you to name what you will let approach.", "judg": "Encounter: the woman is strong. It is not advisable to marry a woman such as this.", "img": "Wind moves beneath the sky: Encounter. Rulers of antiquity took this image and used it to issue their commands, proclaiming them to the four quarters.", "lines": [{"t": "Restraint at first contact", "x": "Tied to a bronze chock that stops the wheel: holding firm brings good fortune. If it goes forward, it meets misfortune. A lean sow, true to its restless nature, strains and paces at the tether."}, {"t": "Guarding what is kept", "x": "The wrapping holds a fish: no blame. It is not favorable toward a guest."}, {"t": "Sore but not seriously at fault", "x": "The buttocks are without skin; walking forward is difficult and hesitant."}, {"t": "Carelessness invites misfortune", "x": "The wrapping holds no fish: this stirs up misfortune."}, {"t": "Hidden excellence, unforced", "x": "Wrapping a melon in willow leaves; excellence held within, unseen. Good fortune falls as though dropped from heaven."}, {"t": "Distance at the horns", "x": "Encounter at the horns: a mark of regret, yet no blame."}]},
{"n": 45, "name": "Convergence", "pin": "Cuì", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Earth", "bits": "000110", "sum": "Convergence describes people, resources, or intentions drawing together around a shared center, and it asks whether that center can hold once the excitement of gathering fades.", "judg": "Convergence: success. The king approaches the ancestral temple. It is fruitful to see the great person; success follows from staying true. A great offering brings good fortune, and it is fruitful to have somewhere to go.", "img": "The lake gathers on the surface of the earth: Convergence. The wise person keeps weapons in good repair and stays alert to what has not yet been foreseen.", "lines": [{"t": "Wavering between huddle and hall", "x": "Sincerity that does not hold to the end brings confusion, then a scattered gathering. If you call out, a small huddle answers with laughter. Do not let that trouble you; going forward brings no blame."}, {"t": "Drawn toward the shared center", "x": "Being drawn toward good fortune brings no blame. Sincerity makes even a modest offering fruitful."}, {"t": "Sighing at the crowd's edge", "x": "Gathering, then sighing: nothing here is gained. Going forward brings no blame, though a small regret remains."}, {"t": "Capability serving the center", "x": "Great good fortune: no blame."}, {"t": "Leadership still earning trust", "x": "Gathering around the one who holds the position: no blame. If trust is not yet complete, lasting steadiness in what is fundamentally right makes regret disappear."}, {"t": "Grief at the outer edge", "x": "Sighing and weeping, tears streaming: no blame."}]},
{"n": 46, "name": "Ascending", "pin": "Shēng", "up": "Earth", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011000", "sum": "Ascending describes growth that succeeds by accumulating small, steady steps rather than by forcing a single dramatic leap toward height.", "judg": "Ascending: great success. It is fitting to seek out the great person; have no anxiety. Advancing toward the south brings good fortune.", "img": "Wood grows within the earth: Ascending. The wise person accords with virtue, building height from an accumulation of small things.", "lines": [{"t": "Sincerity clears the way", "x": "Sincere ascending: great good fortune."}, {"t": "A modest offering suffices", "x": "Sincerity makes even a simple offering fitting: no blame."}, {"t": "The way stands open", "x": "Ascending into an open, undefended town."}, {"t": "Devotion before ambition", "x": "The king makes an offering at Mount Qi: good fortune, no blame."}, {"t": "Arriving by the proper steps", "x": "Staying true brings good fortune: ascending by the steps."}, {"t": "Climbing past the point of use", "x": "Ascending into obscurity: fitting only for a steadfastness that does not cease."}]},
{"n": 47, "name": "Adversity", "pin": "Kùn", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010110", "sum": "Hexagram 47 shows genuine strength hemmed in by real limits: the way through is inner integrity that neither denies the confinement nor collapses under it.", "judg": "Adversity: success remains possible. Staying true matters. A person of substance meets it with good fortune and no blame. Words offered now will not be believed.", "img": "The lake stands over water yet holds none: Adversity. The wise person, even at the furthest edge of what circumstance allows, holds a course and carries the intention through.", "lines": [{"t": "Hiding in the shadow", "x": "Sitting cramped on a bare stump, retreating into a hidden valley: unseen for three years."}, {"t": "Trapped by comfort's offer", "x": "Hemmed in by wine and food, while a scarlet sash of rank is being offered: favorable to hold to ceremony and sincerity; advancing brings misfortune, yet no lasting blame."}, {"t": "Pressed against stone", "x": "Pressed against stone, then leaning on brambles for support; entering one's own house and finding the spouse gone: misfortune."}, {"t": "Slow approach to the block", "x": "Approaching slowly, held back by a bronze carriage; difficulty now, yet the matter reaches a good end."}, {"t": "Wounded yet freed by sincerity", "x": "Wounded and cut off, hemmed in even while wearing the scarlet sash of high office; relief comes gradually - favorable to hold to devotion and ceremony."}, {"t": "Tangled vines, timely move", "x": "Tangled in kudzu vines, standing on unsteady ground: to move is regretted, yet regret is already present - moving forward now brings good fortune."}]},
{"n": 48, "name": "Village Well", "pin": "Jǐng", "up": "Water", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011010", "sum": "Hexagram 48 describes a resource that stays fixed in place while people come and go, and warns that a task left almost finished still fails.", "judg": "The Well: a town may be moved, but its well cannot be moved. It is not diminished by drawing and not increased by rest; those who come and those who go all draw from it. But if the rope almost reaches the water and the jug is not yet raised, and the jug breaks, that is misfortune.", "img": "Water rises above wood: the Well. The wise person organizes the people's labor and encourages them to help one another.", "lines": [{"t": "The silted, disused well", "x": "The well is silted with mud and cannot be drawn from; an old, disused well attracts no birds at all."}, {"t": "Water leaking to the small fish", "x": "The well leaks sideways into a hollow, feeding only the small fish there; the jar is cracked and lets its water drain away."}, {"t": "Cleared, clean, and still unused", "x": "The well has been cleared and cleaned, yet still no one draws from it; this grieves my heart, for it is fit to be used. When the ruler is clear-sighted, everyone shares in its benefit."}, {"t": "Lining the shaft carefully", "x": "The well is lined and its walls set in order: no blame."}, {"t": "Cold, clear water at last", "x": "The well runs clear; its cold spring water is fit to drink."}, {"t": "The well-head left open", "x": "The well is drawn from and left uncovered, open to all; sincerity brings supreme good fortune."}]},
{"n": 49, "name": "Radical Change", "pin": "Gé", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101110", "sum": "Radical Change asks whether the old form has stopped serving its purpose and a new one has earned enough trust to replace it.", "judg": "Radical Change: only once the appointed day has come does trust follow. Great success. It is fruitful to stay true. Regret fades.", "img": "Fire burns within the lake: Radical Change. The wise person studies the calendar and makes the seasons clear.", "lines": [{"t": "Hold fast before acting", "x": "Bind it fast with the hide of a yellow ox."}, {"t": "The appointed day arrives", "x": "Only once the appointed day has come does he change it. To advance now brings good fortune; there is no blame."}, {"t": "The case argued three times", "x": "To advance brings misfortune; even staying true is dangerous. Only when the case for change has been argued three times over does trust arrive."}, {"t": "The mandate renewed", "x": "Regret fades. Trust is present; the mandate is renewed. Good fortune."}, {"t": "Change like a tiger", "x": "The great person changes like a tiger renewing its stripes; before any divination is asked, trust is already there."}, {"t": "Stripes, spots, and mere faces", "x": "The wise person changes like a leopard renewing its spots; the common person merely changes face. To advance brings misfortune; to stay settled and true brings good fortune."}]},
{"n": 50, "name": "Cauldron", "pin": "Dǐng", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011101", "sum": "Hexagram 50 describes a vessel set upright and fed from below, turning raw material into something refined enough to nourish others.", "judg": "The Cauldron: supreme good fortune. Success.", "img": "Fire rests above wood: the Cauldron. The wise person settles into a rightful position and holds firm to what has been entrusted.", "lines": [{"t": "The cauldron tips to empty out", "x": "The cauldron tips over on its legs; but this is useful for pouring out what had gone stale inside it. It is like taking a concubine for the sake of the son she bears: no blame."}, {"t": "Real substance, no rival close enough", "x": "The cauldron holds real substance. My rival is troubled by an ailment and cannot come near me: good fortune."}, {"t": "Good contents, a broken handle", "x": "The cauldron's ears are altered, so it cannot be carried; its rich pheasant meat goes unserved. But when the rain finally comes, the regret lessens, and the end is good fortune."}, {"t": "Legs break under too much weight", "x": "The cauldron's legs break, spilling the ruler's stew; it is soaked and ruined: misfortune."}, {"t": "Yellow ears, a golden rod", "x": "The cauldron has yellow ears and a golden carrying rod: it is fruitful to stay true."}, {"t": "A jade rod completes the work", "x": "The cauldron has a jade carrying rod: supreme good fortune, nothing that is not beneficial."}]},
{"n": 51, "name": "Shock", "pin": "Zhèn", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Thunder", "bits": "100100", "sum": "Shock strikes without warning and shakes you loose from routine, and the figure's whole counsel is to let the startle sharpen your attention rather than scatter it.", "judg": "Shock: success. When the thunder comes, it startles and startles again; then laughter and easy talk follow. The shock terrifies for a hundred miles, and still the sacrificial ladle and wine are not spilled.", "img": "Repeated thunder: Shock. The wise person, in fear and trembling, examines and cultivates themselves.", "lines": [{"t": "The first crack, then laughter", "x": "The thunder comes and startles deeply; afterward come laughter and easy talk: good fortune."}, {"t": "Climbing clear of a loss", "x": "The thunder comes with danger; a great store of goods seems lost, and one climbs to the ninth hill to escape it. Do not chase after the loss - in seven days it is recovered."}, {"t": "Moving forward through the daze", "x": "The thunder leaves one dazed and unsteady; if one moves forward because of the shock rather than freezing before it, there is no fault."}, {"t": "The shock that sinks into mud", "x": "The thunder ends by sinking into the mud."}, {"t": "Danger recurring, nothing truly lost", "x": "The thunder goes and comes, each time with danger; yet nothing of great value is actually lost, and there is still work to attend to."}, {"t": "Trembling at the edge", "x": "The thunder leaves one trembling and drained, glancing about wide-eyed; to press forward now brings misfortune. But if the thunder strikes one's neighbor and not oneself directly, there is no blame - though there will be talk between the parties bound by marriage."}]},
{"n": 52, "name": "Stillness", "pin": "Gèn", "up": "Mountain", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001001", "sum": "Stillness asks you to stop moving on cue, the way a back cannot see the body it belongs to, so attention settles inward instead of chasing every passing stimulus.", "judg": "Stillness: still the back, so the body itself is not seen. Walking through the courtyard, one does not notice the people there. No blame.", "img": "Mountains joined together: Stillness. The wise person keeps thought from wandering beyond one's own place.", "lines": [{"t": "Stillness at the very first step", "x": "Still the toes: no blame. It is fruitful to stay true over the long term."}, {"t": "Unable to rescue what it follows", "x": "Still the calves, but cannot rescue what they are meant to follow: the heart is not at ease."}, {"t": "Forcing a halt at the center", "x": "Still the waist, splitting the spine along its length: danger scorches the heart."}, {"t": "Stillness reaches the whole body", "x": "Still the torso: no blame."}, {"t": "Ordered words, fading regret", "x": "Still the jaw: words come in proper order, and regret fades."}, {"t": "Generous stillness at the summit", "x": "Generous stillness: good fortune."}]},
{"n": 53, "name": "Gradual Advance", "pin": "Jiàn", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001011", "sum": "Gradual Advance asks whether you are willing to let a goal arrive in its proper stages instead of forcing it before the ground beneath it is ready.", "judg": "Gradual Advance: a woman's marriage brings good fortune, when each stage is allowed its proper order. It is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "A tree grows on the mountain: Gradual Advance. The wise person settles into worthy character and steadily improves the customs around them.", "lines": [{"t": "The young goose at the riverbank", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually to the riverbank. The young one is exposed to danger; there is talk about it, but no blame."}, {"t": "Resting on the flat rock", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually to the flat rock. It eats and drinks in quiet contentment. Good fortune."}, {"t": "The plain reached too soon", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually to the high plain - too quickly for its stage. The husband goes forth and does not return; the wife conceives but does not carry to term. Misfortune. It is fruitful to guard against plunderers."}, {"t": "A level branch in the tree", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually to the tree. It may find a level branch to rest on. No blame."}, {"t": "The long wait on the ridge", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually to the high ridge. For three years the wife does not conceive, but in the end nothing overcomes her. Good fortune."}, {"t": "Feathers fit for ceremony", "x": "The wild goose advances gradually into the high cloud paths. Its feathers can be used for ceremony. Good fortune."}]},
{"n": 54, "name": "Young Bride", "pin": "Guīmèi", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110100", "sum": "The marrying maiden warns that a bond formed out of its proper order or season rarely holds, and asks you to test form and timing before committing further.", "judg": "Young Bride: to press forward brings misfortune; no gain lies in continued pursuit.", "img": "Thunder over the lake: Young Bride. The wise person, looking toward what should last to the end, learns to recognize what will wear thin and fail.", "lines": [{"t": "A modest role well filled", "x": "The bride is married off as an attendant to her sister; like someone lame who can still walk, going forward brings good fortune."}, {"t": "Seeing clearly despite limits", "x": "Like someone with impaired sight who can still see, it is fruitful for a person living apart from the crowd to hold to what is correct."}, {"t": "Waiting, then settling for less", "x": "The bride waits as one still unclaimed, and turns back to be married off only as an attendant after all."}, {"t": "A late marriage has its time", "x": "The bride's marriage passes its expected date; a late marriage still has its proper time."}, {"t": "Plain sleeves, real virtue", "x": "When Emperor Yi married off his younger sister, the princess's own sleeves were plainer than her attendant's; like the moon nearly at its full, this brings good fortune."}, {"t": "An empty basket, a bloodless offering", "x": "The woman holds up a basket that has nothing in it; the man cuts the sheep and draws no blood - no gain lies in this at all."}]},
{"n": 55, "name": "Plenty", "pin": "Fēng", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101100", "sum": "Hexagram 55 describes a moment of full plenty that carries its own shadow, calling for clear judgment and decisive action before brightness dims.", "judg": "Plenty: success. The ruler arrives at this moment fully. Do not be anxious; it suits the brightness of the sun at noon.", "img": "Thunder and lightning arrive together: Plenty. The wise person settles disputes and carries out judgments with the same combined clarity and resolve.", "lines": [{"t": "An early, well-matched partner", "x": "He meets his matching partner. Even through a full ten-day span there is no blame; moving forward earns recognition."}, {"t": "Brightness screened, then restored", "x": "His plenty is screened by matted awning; at noon the Dipper is seen."}, {"t": "A costly loss, no blame", "x": "His plenty is curtained by heavy drapery; at noon faint stars are seen. He breaks his right arm: no blame."}, {"t": "An equal, not a superior", "x": "His plenty is screened by matted awning; at noon the Dipper is seen. He meets an equal partner: good fortune."}, {"t": "Inviting brilliance in", "x": "He brings in brilliance; blessing and praise follow: good fortune."}, {"t": "A grand house, empty inside", "x": "He enlarges his house until it screens his own household. Peering through the door, he finds it silent and empty; for three years no one is seen: misfortune."}]},
{"n": 56, "name": "Sojourning", "pin": "Lǚ", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001101", "sum": "Sojourning describes a traveler with no fixed base: modest conduct, tact, and staying true earn only a small, provisional success until you find firm ground again.", "judg": "Sojourning: modest success. Staying true while traveling brings good fortune.", "img": "Fire rests on the mountain: Sojourning. Seeing this, the wise person applies judgment with clarity and caution, and lets no case linger unresolved.", "lines": [{"t": "Petty conduct invites trouble", "x": "Sojourning, petty and small-minded. This is exactly what invites misfortune."}, {"t": "Provisions and a loyal ally", "x": "Sojourning, reaching a lodging. Carrying enough provisions, gaining a loyal attendant. Staying true."}, {"t": "The lodging burns down", "x": "Sojourning, the lodging burns down. Losing the loyal attendant. Even staying true, there is danger."}, {"t": "Provisioned, yet uneasy", "x": "Sojourning, finding a place to stay. Gaining provisions and a hatchet, yet my heart is not at ease."}, {"t": "A costly effort, honored", "x": "Shooting a pheasant, one arrow lost. In the end this brings honor and recognition."}, {"t": "Laughter turns to loss", "x": "The bird's nest burns. The traveler first laughs, then wails and weeps."}]},
{"n": 57, "name": "Wind", "pin": "Xùn", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Wind", "bits": "011011", "sum": "Wind asks whether an intention can spread the way moving air does - gently, repeatedly, entering every gap - instead of forcing itself through by a single loud command.", "judg": "Wind: modest success. It is fruitful to have somewhere to go. It is fruitful to see the great person.", "img": "Wind follows wind: this is Wind. The wise person repeats the instruction and carries it into action.", "lines": [{"t": "Hesitating at the threshold", "x": "Advancing and retreating: it is fruitful to hold the steadiness of a soldier."}, {"t": "Thorough attention under the bed", "x": "Gentleness reaches under the bed. Using diviners and priests in great number brings good fortune and no blame."}, {"t": "Repetition born of anxiety", "x": "Repeated, anxious gentleness: regret."}, {"t": "The hunt rewards patience", "x": "Regret fades. On the hunt, three grades of game are taken."}, {"t": "A weak start, a strong finish", "x": "Staying true brings good fortune; regret fades; nothing is without benefit."}, {"t": "Gentleness past its limit", "x": "Gentleness reaches under the bed; its resources and its resolve are lost."}]},
{"n": 58, "name": "Lake", "pin": "Duì", "up": "Lake", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110110", "sum": "Hexagram 58 shows joy that spreads outward like two lakes feeding each other: lasting pleasure comes from sincerity and mutual exchange, not from chasing approval or flattering what pleases you.", "judg": "Lake: success. It is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "Two lakes joined together, each feeding the other without draining it: Lake. The wise person gathers friends to talk through what has been learned and to practice it together.", "lines": [{"t": "Joy with no agenda", "x": "Joy in harmony: good fortune."}, {"t": "Sincerity outlasts doubt", "x": "Joy held in sincerity: good fortune, and regret fades."}, {"t": "Chased joy turns hollow", "x": "Joy that comes seeking you out: misfortune."}, {"t": "Weighing where joy belongs", "x": "Weighing where joy truly lies brings no rest; guarding against the flaw brings gladness."}, {"t": "Trust placed in decline", "x": "Trusting what is already eroding: danger."}, {"t": "Joy drawn to its edge", "x": "Joy drawn onward."}]},
{"n": 59, "name": "Scattering", "pin": "Huàn", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010011", "sum": "Scattering describes breaking up a frozen or divided condition - dispersing the ice around a stuck situation so trust and movement can flow again.", "judg": "Scattering: success. The king approaches his ancestral temple. It is fruitful to cross the great river. It is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "Wind moves over water: Scattering. The ancient kings made offerings to the Highest and established the ancestral temple.", "lines": [{"t": "Rescue at the first sign", "x": "Using a strong horse to give rescue: good fortune."}, {"t": "Running toward shelter", "x": "In the scattering, hurrying to a resting post: regret fades."}, {"t": "Letting go of self-interest", "x": "Scattering what concerns only oneself: no regret."}, {"t": "Dissolving the faction", "x": "Scattering the clique: great good fortune. The scattering gathers into a hill - a result beyond ordinary reckoning."}, {"t": "The king's own hoard", "x": "Scattering like sweat with a great proclamation; scattering the king's own hoard: no blame."}, {"t": "Scattering the blood, withdrawing far", "x": "Scattering the blood, letting it go, withdrawing far off: no blame."}]},
{"n": 60, "name": "Restraint", "pin": "Jié", "up": "Water", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110010", "sum": "Restraint describes success that depends on a measured limit: a boundary held with proportion protects a resource, while a boundary held too hard turns bitter.", "judg": "Restraint: success. A bitter restraint cannot be sustained.", "img": "Water rests above the lake: Restraint. The wise person sets clear measures and standards, and weighs conduct and character against them.", "lines": [{"t": "Staying inside the inner door", "x": "Not going out beyond the inner door and courtyard: no blame."}, {"t": "Staying in past the moment", "x": "Not going out beyond the outer gate and courtyard: misfortune."}, {"t": "Regret at a restraint not kept", "x": "Failing to restrain oneself brings sighing and regret; no blame follows once the fault is felt."}, {"t": "A boundary kept without strain", "x": "Restraint held at ease: success."}, {"t": "A restraint held sweetly", "x": "A sweet restraint: good fortune. Moving forward brings esteem."}, {"t": "A restraint gripped too hard", "x": "A bitter restraint: persisting in it brings misfortune, yet regret fades."}]},
{"n": 61, "name": "Heartfelt Trust", "pin": "Zhōngfú", "up": "Wind", "lo": "Lake", "bits": "110011", "sum": "Heartfelt Trust describes a sincerity so genuine it can move even the simplest creatures, asking you to prove conviction through patient, consistent contact rather than persuasion.", "judg": "Heartfelt Trust: even pigs and fish respond - good fortune. It is fruitful to cross the great river. It is fruitful to stay true.", "img": "Wind moves over the lake: Heartfelt Trust. The wise person reviews judgments with care and delays a sentence of death.", "lines": [{"t": "Watchful stillness below", "x": "Vigilance brings good fortune; turning toward another brings no rest."}, {"t": "A genuine call answered", "x": "A crane calls in the shade; its young answers it. I have a fine cup; let us share it together."}, {"t": "Unsteady between drumming and song", "x": "Meeting a rival: now advancing, now stopping; now weeping, now singing."}, {"t": "Letting go of the old pair", "x": "The moon nearly full; the paired horse is lost: no blame."}, {"t": "Trust that binds firmly", "x": "Sincerity binds firmly together: no blame."}, {"t": "A voice that outruns its ground", "x": "The cock's crow rises toward heaven; persisting in this brings misfortune."}]},
{"n": 62, "name": "Small Exceeding", "pin": "Xiǎoguò", "up": "Thunder", "lo": "Mountain", "bits": "001100", "sum": "Small Exceeding favors modest, careful action inside a limited scope: attend closely to small matters, stay near the ground, and let bigger ambitions wait for firmer support.", "judg": "Small Exceeding: success. It is fruitful to stay true. Fitting for small matters, not fitting for great undertakings. A flying bird leaves behind only its cry: not fitting to rise, fitting to descend. Great good fortune.", "img": "Thunder above the mountain: Small Exceeding. In conduct, the wise person leans toward too much reverence; in mourning, leans toward too much grief; in spending, leans toward too much frugality.", "lines": [{"t": "A bird that flies too far", "x": "The flying bird brings misfortune."}, {"t": "Meeting the fitting rank", "x": "Passing the grandfather, meeting the grandmother; not reaching the ruler, meeting the minister: no blame."}, {"t": "A guard that is not thorough", "x": "Without guarding thoroughly enough against it, one may be followed and struck down: misfortune."}, {"t": "Restraint that avoids the clash", "x": "No blame. Not overreaching, one meets circumstances as they are. To advance now brings danger - stay on guard. Do not act. Persevere in constancy."}, {"t": "Clouds that will not yet break", "x": "Dense clouds, no rain, gathering from our western outskirts. The duke shoots and takes the one hidden in the cave."}, {"t": "Flying past the point of return", "x": "Failing to be met, one exceeds it still; the flying bird departs from it: misfortune. This is called calamity and disaster."}]},
{"n": 63, "name": "Already Crossed", "pin": "Jìjì", "up": "Water", "lo": "Fire", "bits": "101010", "sum": "Already Crossed describes a task just finished and working well, which succeeds now only because small, steady care keeps the early order from sliding back into disorder.", "judg": "Already Crossed: success, small gains from persisting. Good fortune at the start, disorder at the end.", "img": "Water rests above fire: Already Crossed. The wise person thinks ahead to what could go wrong and guards against it before it arrives.", "lines": [{"t": "Holding the wheel back", "x": "Dragging back the wheel, wetting the tail: no blame."}, {"t": "Losing something small, not chasing it", "x": "The woman loses the screen of her carriage; do not chase after it - within seven days it is recovered."}, {"t": "A long campaign against real resistance", "x": "High Zong campaigns against the Devil's Land; three years pass before it is conquered. Do not employ small-minded people in it."}, {"t": "Guarding the leak all day", "x": "Fine silk kept next to old patched rags for stopping a leak: stay on guard the whole day through."}, {"t": "A modest offering outweighs display", "x": "The eastern neighbor slaughters an ox; it is not equal to the western neighbor's modest offering, which truly receives the blessing."}, {"t": "The wet head of neglect", "x": "The head gets wet: danger."}]},
{"n": 64, "name": "Not Yet Crossed", "pin": "Wèijì", "up": "Fire", "lo": "Water", "bits": "010101", "sum": "Not Yet Crossed describes a task or goal close to succeeding but not there yet, warning that a crossing almost made can still fail in its very last, overconfident step.", "judg": "Not Yet Crossed brings success, yet caution is required: a small fox wades nearly all the way across the stream, then wets its tail at the very end - nothing is gained by rushing the last step.", "img": "Fire sits above water: this is the image of Not Yet Crossed. Seeing it, the wise person carefully distinguishes each thing and settles it in its rightful place.", "lines": [{"t": "Wetting the Tail Too Soon", "x": "Wetting its tail: a small regret."}, {"t": "Braking the Wheel", "x": "Dragging back its wheel: firm and fortunate."}, {"t": "Forcing the Crossing", "x": "Not yet crossed - advancing brings misfortune, yet it is fitting to cross the great river."}, {"t": "Campaign Against the Distant Foe", "x": "Firm and fortunate, regret dissolving: a campaign stirred up against the distant tribes of Guifang, and in three years reward comes from the great state."}, {"t": "Central Brightness at Rest", "x": "Firm and fortunate, without regret: the brightness of a person of true character, sincerity held true - good fortune."}, {"t": "Trust Turning to Excess", "x": "Trust shared over wine: no blame. But wetting the head loses exactly what that trust was for."}]}
];
